"use strict";(self.webpackChunksayhii_portal_documentation=self.webpackChunksayhii_portal_documentation||[]).push([[8130],{7735:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"v1.1.0","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/v1.1.0","source":"@site/blog/2026-03-27-sayhii-feature-release-v1.1.0.md","title":"User and Department Management Features","description":"We\'ve heard from organizations that user and department management can be one of the most time-consuming parts of getting sayhii set up well. It matters because the right user list, department memberships, and department hierarchy all affect how questions are delivered and how reporting is organized.","date":"2026-03-27T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"sayhii","permalink":"/blog/tags/sayhii","description":"sayhii core functionality"}],"readingTime":1.47,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"David Russell","title":"CTO @ sayhii","url":"https://sayhii.io","page":{"permalink":"/blog/authors/drussell"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/david-russell-52aa982b/","bluesky":"https://bsky.app/profile/sayhii-dpr.bsky.social"},"imageURL":"/img/DavidSquareHeadshot.png","key":"drussell"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v1.1.0","title":"User and Department Management Features","authors":["drussell"],"tags":["sayhii"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"New Features for sayhii","permalink":"/blog/v0.8.0"}},"content":"We\'ve heard from organizations that user and department management can be one of the most time-consuming parts of getting sayhii set up well. It matters because the right user list, department memberships, and department hierarchy all affect how questions are delivered and how reporting is organized.\\n\\nLooking ahead, we also want to give organizations more control over how different departments experience sayhii. You could imagine, for example, using different question phrasing for people in accounting than for people on the manufacturing floor.\\n\\nWith this release, we\'ve added a new interface to make it easier to manage your users, your department hierarchy, and user memberships in departments.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nFor full details, you\'ll want to refer to the documentation, but here are the highlights.\\n\\n## User Management\\n\\nOn the [Organization page](/docs/portal-admin/organization) in the admin portal, you can now add individual users without first creating a CSV file to upload. You can also edit existing users directly, including details like manager, department, and role.\\n\\n## Department Management\\n\\nsayhii administrators can now create a custom department hierarchy for their organization.\\n\\nIf your organization uses an [HRIS integration](/docs/portal-settings/hris-integration), you can import groups from your HRIS into the hierarchy or map HRIS groups to departments you\'ve already defined in sayhii.\\n\\nIf you aren\'t using an HRIS, you can still configure the hierarchy manually and map users from your file uploads into the right departments.\\n\\nThis gives you more control over how reporting is structured across your organization.\\n\\nDepartment management is currently in beta and available by request.\\n\\n## Thanks for being here\\n\\nThanks for reading. We hope these new tools make it easier to keep your sayhii organization up to date and your reporting structure aligned with the way your team actually works."},{"id":"v0.8.0","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/v0.8.0","source":"@site/blog/2025-05-10-sayhii-feature-release-v0.8.0.md","title":"New Features for sayhii","description":"We\'ve been working hard to update sayhii and improve our platform to better meet the needs of our customers. Two of the most common questions we hear are:","date":"2025-05-10T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"sayhii","permalink":"/blog/tags/sayhii","description":"sayhii core functionality"}],"readingTime":2.93,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"David Russell","title":"CTO @ sayhii","url":"https://sayhii.io","page":{"permalink":"/blog/authors/drussell"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/david-russell-52aa982b/","bluesky":"https://bsky.app/profile/sayhii-dpr.bsky.social"},"imageURL":"/img/DavidSquareHeadshot.png","key":"drussell"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v0.8.0","title":"New Features for sayhii","authors":["drussell"],"tags":["sayhii"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"User and Department Management Features","permalink":"/blog/v1.1.0"},"nextItem":{"title":"The Connection Between Engagement and Skill Development","permalink":"/blog/engagement-and-skill-development"}},"content":"We\'ve been working hard to update sayhii and improve our platform to better meet the needs of our customers. Two of the most common questions we hear are:\\n\\n- Can employees answer questions on a web page so we don\'t have to install the sayhii desktop app?\\n- Can we ask our own questions instead of just the standard sayhii questions?\\n\\nWith our latest release, we\'re excited to say the answer to both is a resounding **YES**!\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nFor full details, you\u2019ll want to refer to the documentation \u2014 but here are the highlights.\\n\\n## Custom Modules\\n\\nA few months ago, we made foundational changes to the sayhii backend to support different types of question sets and new algorithms for selecting the next best question for each user. Internally, we\'ve called this work **modularization**. Our first major feature built on this foundation is support for **Custom Modules**.\\n\\nCustom Modules allow you to define a specific set of questions you\'d like to ask your employees. sayhii handles the delivery, and you\'ll receive aggregate results broken down by department. We also highlight which questions received the highest and lowest average scores to help you spot trends quickly.\\n\\nJust like our standard questions, Custom Modules maintain full anonymity for respondents \u2014 so employees can feel just as confident and safe when sharing their feedback.\\n\\nThis is a great way to build on the daily habit sayhii helps cultivate and gather insight on questions specific to your organization.\\n\\nCheck out the [sayhii documentation](/docs/portal-admin/custom-modules) for more details, including a video walkthrough of creating your first custom module.\\n\\n## Module Scheduling\\n\\nOnce you\'ve created a **Custom Module**, you can decide when you\'d like those questions to be sent to users. These questions are delivered *in addition to* the standard daily sayhii questions.\\n\\nTo help avoid question overload:\\n\\n- Only one module can be scheduled at a time\\n- No more than one question per day will be delivered from a scheduled module\\n\\nFor now, you can only schedule the modules you\'ve created. In the future, we plan to offer prebuilt sayhii modules you can schedule to explore specific topics or assess different areas of your organization.\\n\\nScheduled modules are managed as part of your organization\'s [Question Plan](/docs/portal-settings/question-plan#scheduled-modules), and that documentation provides additional guidance.\\n\\n## Questions in the Portal\\n\\nSome organizations have employees who can\u2019t use the desktop application for various reasons. We\'ve been working to meet users where they are \u2014 and our first step is bringing the sayhii question experience directly into the sayhii Portal.\\n\\nWhen this feature is enabled, users will be prompted with the current question \u2014 if they haven\'t already answered that day \u2014 as soon as they log in to the Portal.\\n\\nWe hope this option allows more employees to participate and ensures that **everyone\'s voice is heard**.\\n\\nIf you\'d like to enable this for your team, you can share this [guide](/docs/portal-everyone/profile#sayhii-questions-in-the-portal) with them to get started.\\n\\n## Documentation\\n\\nIf you\'re reading this, you\u2019ve already found our new [Documentation Site](/)! We hope it\u2019s helpful as you explore what sayhii can do \u2014 especially when it comes to understanding the insights we surface. We\'ll keep this site up to date with the latest changes, with a focus on the technical side of using sayhii.\\n\\n## Thanks for Reading\\n\\nIf you\u2019ve made it this far \u2014 thank you! We\u2019re excited to bring these new features to you, and we hope they make sayhii even more valuable in helping employees engage with your organization."},{"id":"engagement-and-skill-development","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/engagement-and-skill-development","source":"@site/blog/2025-04-24-the-connection-between-engagement-and-skill-development/index.md","title":"The Connection Between Engagement and Skill Development","description":"Technology is rapidly evolving, industries are transforming overnight, and one truth remains constant: engaged individuals learn faster, retain more, and develop deeper skills. Whether in the workplace, the classroom, or personal growth, engagement fuels the development of expertise, making learning both meaningful and sustainable.","date":"2025-04-24T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Thought Leadership","permalink":"/blog/tags/thought-leadership","description":"We share out thoughts on the future of work and how to get there."},{"inline":false,"label":"Skill Development","permalink":"/blog/tags/skill-development","description":"How can we help you develop your skills?"}],"readingTime":3.76,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Amy Gurske","title":"Founder/CEO @ sayhii","url":"https://sayhii.io","page":{"permalink":"/blog/authors/agurske"},"socials":{"linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/\u2728amy-gurske-6a04974/","bluesky":"https://bsky.app/profile/sayhii.io"},"imageURL":"/img/AmySquareHeadshot.png","key":"agurske"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"engagement-and-skill-development","title":"The Connection Between Engagement and Skill Development","authors":["agurske"],"tags":["thought leadership","skill development"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"New Features for sayhii","permalink":"/blog/v0.8.0"}},"content":"Technology is rapidly evolving, industries are transforming overnight, and one truth remains constant: engaged individuals learn faster, retain more, and develop deeper skills. Whether in the workplace, the classroom, or personal growth, engagement fuels the development of expertise, making learning both meaningful and sustainable.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Engagement: The Catalyst for Growth\\n\\nEngagement is more than just showing up\u2014it\u2019s about being emotionally and intellectually invested in a task. When people are engaged, they are curious, persistent, and willing to explore new challenges. This deep involvement creates an optimal state for learning, where skills are not only acquired but also applied and refined in real-world contexts.\\n\\nEngagement thrives in environments that are:\\n\\n1. **Stimulating** \u2013 Presenting new challenges and opportunities.\\n\\n2. **Purpose-Driven** \u2013 Connecting tasks to a larger mission or personal goal.\\n\\n3. **Interactive** \u2013 Encouraging participation, feedback, and collaboration.\\n\\n4. **Autonomous** \u2013 Allowing individuals to take ownership of their learning.\\n\\n## The Neuroscience of Engagement and Learning\\n\\nNeuroscience has shown that engagement enhances neuroplasticity\u2014the brain\u2019s ability to form and strengthen neural connections. When individuals are engaged, dopamine, a neurotransmitter linked to motivation and reward, is released, reinforcing learning pathways and making skill acquisition not only faster but also more enjoyable.\\n\\nThe brain\'s frontal cortex, responsible for executive functions such as problem-solving, focus, and decision-making, plays a crucial role in engagement. When individuals are deeply involved in a task, the frontal cortex is highly active, directing attention and organizing information in a way that supports deeper learning. On the other hand, the rear cortex, which processes sensory input and helps contextualize experiences, works in tandem with the frontal cortex to integrate new knowledge with existing frameworks. This collaboration between the two regions strengthens comprehension and retention.\\n\\n![unstressed vs. stressed brain function](./060620_LS_inline-2-brains_desktop.jpg)\\n\\nFurthermore, engaged learners enter a state of \\"flow,\\" as described by psychologist Mihaly Csikszentmihalyi. In this state, the frontal cortex remains highly active while non-essential mental distractions fade into the background. The rear cortex simultaneously processes environmental cues with heightened efficiency, allowing individuals to become fully immersed in their work, losing track of time and performing at their highest potential. Flow optimizes learning, reinforcing skill development through continuous challenge and feedback while maintaining an ideal balance between focus and creativity.\\n\\n## How Engagement Drives Skill Development\\n\\n1. **Active Participation Enhances Retention** - Studies have shown that passive learning\u2014such as listening to lectures or reading without interaction\u2014results in lower retention rates. In contrast, hands-on engagement, such as solving problems, working on projects, or engaging in discussion, leads to deeper understanding and long-term skill mastery.\\n\\n2. **Engagement Builds Adaptive Expertise** - A highly engaged individual doesn\u2019t just learn a skill; they learn how to adapt it to different situations. This ability to transfer knowledge across various domains is critical in today\u2019s rapidly changing workforce, where employees must continuously evolve with emerging technologies and market trends.\\n\\n3. **Emotional Investment Strengthens Commitment** - When individuals feel a personal connection to what they are learning, they are more likely to persist through challenges. A student passionate about coding, for example, will spend hours debugging a program, refining their logic, and seeking improvement\u2014not because they have to, but because they are internally driven to do so.\\n\\n4. **Collaboration and Social Learning Accelerate Growth** - Engagement is amplified in environments where learners can collaborate, exchange ideas, and receive feedback. Whether in a corporate training session or an online course, learning alongside others fosters deeper comprehension, exposes individuals to new perspectives, and reinforces skills through discussion and peer interaction.\\n\\n## Bridging Engagement and Skill Development in Organizations\\n\\nLeaders and educators can foster engagement-driven learning environments by:\\n\\n- **Creating Real-World Challenges** \u2013 Providing opportunities for employees or students to work on meaningful, practical problems.\\n\\n- **Encouraging Autonomy** \u2013 Giving individuals the freedom to explore, experiment, and take ownership of their learning journey.\\n\\n- **Recognizing and Rewarding Growth** \u2013 Celebrating progress and providing incentives for continued development.\\n\\n- **Investing in Interactive Learning Tools** \u2013 Leveraging technology, gamification, and collaborative platforms to make learning more immersive.\\n\\nFinal Thoughts: Engagement is the Key to Mastery\\nSkill development isn\u2019t just about knowledge acquisition\u2014it\u2019s about fostering curiosity, resilience, and a passion for growth. Engagement is the bridge that connects learning with mastery, ensuring that individuals not only develop new skills but also have the motivation and mindset to apply them effectively.\\n\\nBy cultivating environments where engagement is prioritized, we unlock the potential for lifelong learning, innovation, and continuous improvement. Whether in the workplace, academia, or personal endeavors, the more engaged we are, the greater our capacity to grow."}]}}')}}]);